## Step 1: Quality Control (FastQC + MultiQC)

### Commands

'FastQC' is a quality control tool that analyzes high-throughput sequencing data to assess sample quality, generating visual reports on base quality scores, adapter contamination, and GC content for individual samples.

Command to activate the Conda environment containing FastQC prior to executing quality analysis on the sample read sets.
```
conda activate snps
```

Create a directory to store the FastQC quality control reports.
```
mkdir 01_fastqc
```

Run 'FastQC' on each sample set within your target directory, specifying '-o .' (the -o flag followed by a space and a period) to output the resulting 'HTML' and zip files to the current directory.
```
fastqc ../../Raw_data/Sample_A_R1.fastq.gz -o . /
```

MultiQC gives a rounded number for total reads and does not report total bases per sample. To find out those numbers use this:

```
for f in *.fastq.gz; do
  echo -ne "$f\t"
  zcat "$f" | awk 'NR%4==2{r++; b+=length($0)} END{printf "%d\t%d\t%.1f\n", r, b, b/r}'
done | column -t
```

This gives the total reads, then the total bases, then the average read length for each file.

